### Zscaler application metrics

The following example requires an existing Zscaler Direct data source and service.
For an Agent data source, change the indicator kind to `Agent`.

{{ tffile "examples/resources/nobl9_slo/zscaler.tf" }}

Supported metrics are `score` (0–100), `pft` and `dns` (milliseconds), and `availability` (percent).
Application and location IDs are positive integers. Omit `location_id` to aggregate across all locations.
These are raw metrics, not good/total counts. The example targets 99% of collected application-score samples above 65,
not 99% of individual users. If ZDX returns only page fetch time for a different requested metric, the query returns no data.

